</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e9ab8ea-c47e-11f1-b3d1-650afb66e3ea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:47:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Powerful 7.6 magnitude quake shakes Panama, triggering tsunami warnings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning</link><description>
A strong 7.6 magnitude earthquake struck near the southern ​coast ‌of Panama ⁠on Friday at a 10 km depth, ‌according to the US Geological ⁠Survey, shaking buildings as far away as the capital and prompting evacuations. The US Tsunami Warning ​System showed potential tsunami threats across much of Central America's Pacific ​coast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e685866-c417-11f1-a54f-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T190605Z-119910366-RC2UZNAG2SLO-RTRMADP-3-PANAMA-QUAKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e685866-c417-11f1-a54f-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T190605Z-119910366-RC2UZNAG2SLO-RTRMADP-3-PANAMA-QUAKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26ce30f4-c410-11f1-bc25-adb65edd2195</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:39:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e685866-c417-11f1-a54f-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T190605Z-119910366-RC2UZNAG2SLO-RTRMADP-3-PANAMA-QUAKE.jpg">© Enea Lebrun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Unweaving Jeffrey Epstein’s web: What the files have revealed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-unweaving-jeffrey-epstein-s-web-what-the-files-have-revealed</link><description>
On January 30, 2026, the US Justice Department released 3 million documents. Photos, videos, emails, text messages, court records... All connected to one man: Jeffrey Epstein. Since then, media outlets around the world have brought to light the vast amount of people that appear in the Epstein files. Eight months on, what what do these revelations tell us about Jeffrey Epstein’s network? How did it operate? FRANCE 24 journalist Ava Luquet spent months digging through the files. In this video, she takes a closer look at what they reveal about the predator’s network and its inner workings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/146a2ab2-c27b-11f1-b11f-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EPSTEIN-EN-vignette-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/146a2ab2-c27b-11f1-b11f-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EPSTEIN-EN-vignette-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c8fad210-c26c-11f1-b49f-dd754fbf8bc3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:00:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pentagon vows to livestream first military execution in decades</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-pentagon-vows-to-livestream-first-military-execution-in-decades</link><description>
The first US military execution in more than 65 years will be livestreamed, announced the Pentagon on Thursday, after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said it would be "public".
 
Former Army psychiatrist Nidal Hasan opened fire at Fort Hood in Texas in 2009, killing 13 people. His execution will take place at the military base on December 3, 2026.
 
 "The livestreaming of an execution is tantamount to a public execution and would breach the absolute prohibition of torture," the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d18288-c3ca-11f1-98a3-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/Nidal-Hasan-execution00.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d18288-c3ca-11f1-98a3-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/Nidal-Hasan-execution00.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcb4c3ae-c3ca-11f1-a485-5fede210fc06</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 10:56:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
